================================================================================

This repository is deliberately MIXED-LICENCE. Apache-2.0 is granted over the
PUBLIC VERIFIER and nothing else. Reading only `LICENSE` would over-state the
grant, which is why this file exists and why it is specific.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
COVERED BY APACHE-2.0 (the public verifier)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  neomundi_evidence/                      the pip package: CLI and metadata
  verifier/verify.py                      archive verifier
  verifier/verify_attestation.py          Ed25519/JWS attestation verifier
  verifier/canonical.py                   canonicalisation profile
  verifier/i18n.py                        translations (optional at runtime)
  verifier/timestamp.py                   OpenTimestamps proof verifier
  verifier/adapters/ingest.py             submission-package verifier
  verifier/verifier-rs/                   second independent verifier (Rust)
  verifier/verifier-rs-crypto/            signature/archive verifier (Rust)

  gateway.py, engine.py                   the input/output gateway
  contracts/                              the gateway's request/response schemas
  tests/, demo/, examples/                tests, demonstration, example requests
  docs/, references/                      documentation of the above

The Python wheel `neomundi-evidence-verify` distributes exactly NINE files:
the three of `neomundi_evidence/` and the SIX verifier files listed above
(`verify`, `verify_attestation`, `canonical`, `i18n`, `timestamp`,
`adapters/ingest`). Measured on the built wheel, each of the six byte-identical
to its source under `verifier/`.

The two Rust crates already carried `license = "Apache-2.0"` in their own
`Cargo.toml` before this notice existed. That earlier declaration is
confirmed, not replaced.

