--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

No third-party source code is vendored in this repository.

The Python package has NO mandatory dependency. Two optional extras are
installed from PyPI by pip — never bundled here — and remain governed by
their own licences:

  cryptography        Apache-2.0 OR BSD-3-Clause
  opentimestamps      LGPL-3.0; pulls python-bitcoinlib (LGPL-3.0)
                      and pycryptodomex (BSD-2-Clause / public domain)

  WARNING: `opentimestamps` is LGPL-3.0. It is optional and separately
  installed, so no copyleft obligation attaches to this work. Never vendor
  it.

`verifier-rs` has no dependency at all: its Cargo.lock holds one entry.
`verifier-rs-crypto` depends at build time on `ed25519-dalek` and its
transitive closure — 22 third-party crates listed in its Cargo.lock, all
permissive (BSD-3-Clause, MIT, Apache-2.0, and Unicode-3.0 for one). They are
not redistributed here, and no compiled binary is distributed. Distributing
one would trigger their attribution requirements.

  Two of those 22 were NOT measured: libc 0.2.191 and fiat-crypto 0.3.0 are
  declared in Cargo.lock but were not fetched by the build performed on
  14 November 2026. They are not assumed. Read them before distributing any
  compiled binary.

